1
00:04:04,615 --> 00:04:10,615
4 times the action. 4 times the adventure. 4 times the fantastic.

2
00:08:09,230 --> 00:08:15,230
Fantastic Four is a action, fantasy, science fiction film directed by Tim Story.

3
00:12:13,846 --> 00:12:19,846
During a space voyage, four scientists are altered by cosmic rays: Reed Richards gains the ability to stretch his body; Sue
Storm can become invisible; Johnny Storm controls fire; and Ben Grimm is turned into a super-strong … thing.

4
00:16:18,461 --> 00:16:24,461
Together, these "Fantastic Four" must now thwart the evil plans of Dr.

5
00:20:23,076 --> 00:20:29,076
Doom and save the world from certain destruction.

6
00:24:27,692 --> 00:24:33,692
Reed Richards / Mr. Fantastic, played by Ioan Gruffudd.

7
00:28:32,307 --> 00:28:38,307
Sue Storm / Invisible Woman, played by Jessica Alba.

8
00:32:36,923 --> 00:32:42,923
Johnny Storm / Human Torch, played by Chris Evans.

9
00:36:41,538 --> 00:36:47,538
Ben Grimm / The Thing, played by Michael Chiklis.

10
00:40:46,153 --> 00:40:52,153
Victor von Doom / Doctor Doom, played by Julian McMahon.

11
00:44:50,769 --> 00:44:56,769
Leonard, played by Hamish Linklater.

12
00:48:55,384 --> 00:49:01,384
Fantastic Four (sometimes stylized as Fantastic 4) is a 2005 superhero film based on
the Marvel Comics superhero team created by Stan Lee and Jack Kirby.

13
00:53:00,000 --> 00:53:06,000
It was directed by Tim Story and written by Mark Frost and Michael France.

14
00:57:04,615 --> 00:57:10,615
The film stars Ioan Gruffudd, Jessica Alba, Chris Evans, Michael
Chiklis, Julian McMahon, and Kerry Washington.

15
01:01:09,230 --> 01:01:15,230
The film follows the origins of the titular team as they learn to come to terms with
their newfound abilities following their exposure to cosmic rays.

16
01:05:13,846 --> 01:05:19,846
This was the second live-action Fantastic Four film to be filmed.

17
01:09:18,461 --> 01:09:24,461
A previous attempt, titled The Fantastic Four, was a B movie
produced by Roger Corman that ultimately went unreleased.

18
01:13:23,076 --> 01:13:29,076
Fantastic Four was released in the United States on July 8, 2005.

19
01:17:27,692 --> 01:17:33,692
The film received generally negative reviews from critics (though Evans and Chiklis's performances
were praised), but has gone through some re-evaluation over the years after its release.

20
01:21:32,307 --> 01:21:38,307
The film grossed $333.5 million worldwide and was a box office success.

21
01:25:36,923 --> 01:25:42,923
A sequel, Fantastic Four: Rise of the Silver Surfer, was released in 2007.

22
01:29:41,538 --> 01:29:47,538
A reboot was released in 2015, while another, set in the Marvel
Cinematic Universe (MCU), was released in 2025.

23
01:33:46,153 --> 01:33:52,153
Evans, who would portray Captain America in the Marvel Cinematic Universe (MCU), later reprised
his role as Johnny Storm / Human Torch in the MCU film Deadpool & Wolverine (2024).

24
01:37:50,769 --> 01:37:56,769
The film explores themes of mask, friendship, marriage
proposal, fire, sibling relationship.

25
01:41:55,384 --> 01:42:01,384
The tone is thought_provoking.
